WEBVTT

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:02.580
MCP stands for Model Context Protocol.

00:00:03.420 --> 00:00:05.380
Fabric provides an API endpoint, so

00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:07.039
enterprise developers can connect their

00:00:07.039 --> 00:00:09.300
own compatible external AI clients

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:11.260
or custom applications to the ontology.

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:11.959
It tells useful.

00:00:12.460 --> 00:00:13.720
However, the current guidance notes

00:00:13.720 --> 00:00:14.699
a severe limitation.

00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:17.280
Service principal access is currently

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:18.680
unavailable for this endpoint.

00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:20.880
Explain that for the non -developers.

00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:22.500
What is a service principal?

00:00:22.759 --> 00:00:24.560
A service principal is basically a

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:27.119
machine identity. It's a non -human

00:00:27.119 --> 00:00:28.780
service account you use, so a

00:00:28.780 --> 00:00:30.880
backend server or an automated script

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:32.740
can talk to an API securely

00:00:32.740 --> 00:00:34.300
without needing a human being to

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:36.220
physically type in a username and

00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:38.120
password. Oh, so you can automate

00:00:38.120 --> 00:00:40.600
it? Right. But because service principal

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:42.160
access is missing in this preview,

00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:43.720
you currently have to authenticate

00:00:43.720 --> 00:00:45.480
as a real human user.

00:00:45.740 --> 00:00:47.280
You cannot easily set up a

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:49.519
fully automated unattended machine

00:00:49.519 --> 00:00:50.739
to machine integration.

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:52.620
That drastically limits how you can

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:54.480
integrate this ontology into automated

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:56.699
backend enterprise systems right now.
